course: dictionary
lesson: 7290
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. The sentence around it tells you which one the writer means. «In pan-pipes the shorter pipes play higher notes and the longer pipes play lower notes.» Here the clue is «play higher notes», so pipe means a musical instrument you blow into.
explain: «The coloured paint marks show where pipes and cables run, so the diggers do not hit them.» Pipes here are hidden tubes under the road that carry water or gas, not music or smoke. Ask yourself: what would fit in this place? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: Pipe can also be a verb, a doing word. «To pipe is to send something through pipes, or to squeeze cream or icing out of a bag.» The phrase «piping hot» means very hot, so context and common phrases both help you.
fact: Pipe is a noun for a long tube that water, gas or oil flows through.
fact: Pipe is also a noun for a small tube with a bowl, used for smoking tobacco.
fact: Pipe is a noun for a simple musical instrument you blow into, like bagpipes or a recorder.
fact: «Piping hot» means very hot, and «pipe up» means to start to speak.
fact: When a word has more than one meaning, read the whole sentence and the words around it before you choose.
exercise: «In pan-pipes the shorter pipes play higher notes and the longer pipes play lower notes.» What kind of pipe is this? | A tube for smoking tobacco | A tube for water | *A musical instrument you blow into | A bag for icing
exercise: «The coloured paint marks show where pipes and cables run, so the diggers do not hit them.» What are pipes here? | Icing bags | Musical instruments | *Long tubes that water or gas flows through, hidden under the road | Long tubes that water or gas flows through
exercise: «A hookah is a tall smoking pipe with water in it.» What is a hookah? | A musical instrument | A kind of icing bag | *A tall pipe for smoking tobacco | A tube under the road
test: Mum says the soup is «piping hot». What does piping hot mean? | Wet from the pipes | *Very hot | Cold and fresh | Playing a tune
test: Anna will pipe the cream onto the cake. What does pipe mean here? | To blow a tune on a flute | To smoke a tobacco pipe | To burst and flood the kitchen | *To squeeze cream out of a bag
exam: Sam is asked a question in class and he will pipe up. What does pipe up mean? | To smoke a pipe | *To start to speak | To play a tune | To burst like a pipe
